; The examples, as the theory MEBI.Examples. Built by `dune build` and CI;
; not part of the opam package (no (package ...)), like test/rocq.
;
; Only the files listed are built: the fast ones (~2 min together). The
; heavy proof files (the Alternating Bit Protocol, Test4, the large CADP
; and evaluation files, the Proc/Test1-3 and CADP proof suites) take
; minutes and gigabytes each: bench/proofs.sh compiles them one at a time,
; under a memory cap, against this build (bench/README.md). Until 2026-11-05
; this list was the uncommented part of _CoqProject, built by make.

(rocq.theory
 (name MEBI.Examples)
 (synopsis "MEBI plugin examples")
 (plugins rocq-mebi.mebi)
 (stdlib yes)
 (theories Stdlib MEBI)
 (modules
  ; CCS (value-free, Milner 1989): textbook pairs and the Alternating Bit
  ; Protocol, and instances of CTrees' CCS laws (~25s)
  CCS
  Bisimilarity.CCS.PluginProofs
  Bisimilarity.CCS.LawProofs
  ; the evaluation levers, small instances (~40s)
  Evaluation.Base
  Evaluation.Width
  Evaluation.Layers
  Evaluation.Depth
  ; Proc, and Test4 under the normalised semantics (82 states)
  Proc
  ProcCongruence
  Bisimilarity.Proc.Test1.Terms
  Bisimilarity.Proc.Test2.Terms
  Bisimilarity.Proc.Test3.Terms
  Bisimilarity.Proc.Test4.Terms
  Bisimilarity.Proc.Test4.NormTermTests
  ; CADP: the models and specifications the proof files use (no plugin
  ; proofs; Norm.v's hand proof ~35s)
  CADP.Model
  CADP.Glued
  CADP.Norm
  CADP.Obs
  CADP.SpecMutex
  CADP.SpecFifo
  CADP.Hidden
  CADP.Terms))

(include_subdirs qualified)
